    "body": "\nSummary:\nPoint the `torch_checkpointing` requirement at the `main` branch of\nmeta-pytorch/torch_checkpointing instead of commit `dcbb3a59`, as #5131 did for\n`spmd_types`. TorchTitan's `TorchCheckpointingManager` is developed alongside\ntorch_checkpointing, so with a commit pin every torch_checkpointing fix needs a\nseparate TorchTitan bump before CI or `pip install -r requirements.txt` sees it.\n\n`requirements.txt` at the repo root is a symlink to this file and\n`pyproject.toml` reads its dependencies from it, so the change applies to pip,\nuv and CI alike. Workflows that install the requirements directly resolve\n`main` on every run; the Docker image resolves it when the image is rebuilt.\n\nTest Plan:\n- The edited requirements file parses with `packaging.requirements.Requirement`;\n  the URL is `git+https://github.com/meta-pytorch/torch_checkpointing.git@main`.\n- `pre-commit run --files .ci/docker/requirements.txt` passes.\n- `pytest tests/unit_tests/cpu/components/checkpointer/` against torch_checkpointing\n  `dcbb3a59`, the current `main`: 121 passed.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
